Maintainer: David Benatia <david.benatia@hec.ca>
Description: Estimates group-time average treatment effects in panels with
    missing outcomes by the chained difference-in-differences of Bellégo,
    Benatia and Dortet-Bernadet (2025) <doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2024.105783>.
    It is a layer on the 'did' package that keeps the att_gt() and aggte()
    interface and adds an estimation mode. Chained estimation, the default for
    panel data, combines short within-unit comparisons by the generalized
    method of moments. It provides chained inverse probability weighting
    (IPW), outcome regression (OR) and doubly robust (DR) estimation, where OR
    and DR use one pooled regression of the controls' outcome changes; custom
    IPW callbacks; correction for covariate-dependent missing outcomes by
    observation weighting, change imputation or their augmented combination;
    parallel trends from each cohort's reference period (PT-post) or from a
    chosen common start date (PT-all); and a chained conditional pretrend test
    through conditional_did_pretest(). Ordinary mode delegates unchanged to
    the Callaway and Sant'Anna (2021) <doi:10.1016/j.jeconom.2020.12.001>
    estimators in 'did'.
